# Line endings. The repository stores text with LF and every checkout uses LF, on Windows too, so a file is never
# "modified" only because of CRLF, the "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning on every commit goes away, and the CI
# (Linux) and the developers' PCs (Windows) agree. Nothing in the existing history is rewritten: the stored files
# already use LF (checked with `git ls-files --eol`).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never converted, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary

# Generated files: collapsed in pull request diffs.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated
